# Development and test artifacts that are never an input to the production deployment: the build
# (`vercel.json`'s `buildCommand`: config-preflight, then `tsr generate`, `tsc -b`, `vite build`)
# and the Python functions under `api/` read none of them. Visual tests and Storybook run in GitHub
# Actions from a git checkout, which this file does not affect. See docs/adr/0002-hosting.md.

# Playwright output (`playwright.config.ts`)
/test-results/
/playwright-report/

# Python tool caches
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Visual-test baselines, tracked in git for `tests/visual/` and `pr.yml`/`baselines.yml`
/packages/design-system/__screenshots__/

# Generated Storybook build (`pnpm --filter design-system build-storybook`)
/packages/design-system/storybook-static/

# Local environment files: the CLI uploads a working copy and does not apply `.gitignore`, so
# without this a production `.env.vercel` would be uploaded. `.env.example` stays: the build's
# `scripts/checks/config-preflight.mjs` reads it.
.env*
!.env.example

# Local agent worktrees and agent configuration: never an input to the build or to a function. The
# CLI uploads a working copy and does not apply `.gitignore`, so without this every worktree under
# `.claude/worktrees/` would be uploaded with the deployment.
/.claude/

# Spec-kit artifacts, documentation and CI workflows: nothing the build (`vercel.json`'s
# `buildCommand`: config-preflight, then the web build) and no function under `api/` reads them.
# `scripts/deploy/ignore-build.mjs` classifies paths from `git diff`, not from the working tree.
/docs/
/specs/
/.specify/
/.github/
